Device updates: site permission caps and credential references
===============================================================

PATCH /devices/{device_id} now applies the resolved device site's permission
cap after the existing organization and site-access checks, before changing any
field. A read-only or unknown site access level cannot update the device even
when the user's role allows device:update. The actual route-level role/API-key
permission dependency remains in place. Denial is 403 for an insufficient cap;
existing out-of-scope device 404 and foreign-organization 403 behavior is retained.

A non-null credential_id must also pass the same site visibility check as the
credential read endpoints, after the existing organization and deleted-row
checks. An inaccessible credential returns Credential not found (404), without
applying other fields in that PATCH. Explicit null still clears a reference;
omitting the field preserves it. No secret is decrypted by this endpoint.

Organization-wide credentials (site_id null), administrator privileges and the
existing grant-less-user hybrid access model remain unchanged. A user granted
both sites can attach a credential across those granted sites. This correction
does not require the credential and device to share one site, migrate existing
links, or change the credential's lifecycle/ownership rules. It does not fix
other device mutation routes or claim that credentials were exfiltrated.

Qualification uses actual PostgreSQL rows, HTTP-ASGI regression tests and an
independent loopback TCP HTTP server. The authenticated CurrentUser is synthetic;
the real route permission dependency and device endpoint run unmodified. Checks
cover forbidden sibling credentials, read/unknown site caps, scoped API-key
ceilings, administrators, grant-less and multi-site callers, missing/deleted/
foreign records, allowed credential clearing and all-field atomic refusal.
No vendor hardware, login/token verification or concurrent grant revocation is
exercised. Public-image and full-system acceptance remain separately recorded.
